@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+# Negotiated compaction lifecycle
+
+ACP v1 clients opt in with `clientCapabilities.session.compaction: {}`. Using
+SDK 1.4.0's public typed session update, the adapter maps runtime compacting
+status to `in_progress`, explicit success or compact boundary to `completed`,
+and explicit compact failure to `failed`. The opening runtime UUID identifies
+the lifecycle; terminal-only updates use the terminal UUID. Duplicate terminal
+statuses and boundary enrichment are quiet; only an unseen start UUID opens a
+new ID. Structured IDs stay fenced across turn resets, including unresolved
+starts, so replay cannot reopen an old entity or change its terminal outcome.
+Observed terminal-message UUIDs are fenced as aliases of the owning compaction,
+including duplicate statuses and boundary enrichment observed before the next
+start. Aliases consume the same bounded ID capacity. Their replay cannot close a
+later compaction. A never-observed UUID cannot be correlated to a previous
+attempt solely from this SDK stream; no such coverage is claimed.
+The consumer retains at most 1,024 IDs and never evicts them. At capacity, it
+suppresses new lifecycle entities and emits one body-free diagnostic warning;
+existing active entities can still terminalize. Summary/result suppression stays
+active even when lifecycle visibility has stopped. Replace the consumer to
+restore visibility; cancellation and coverage policy are unchanged.
+
+Unsupported, null, or malformed capabilities retain the existing synthetic tool
+lifecycle. The negotiated path sends no summary or raw error/metadata payload.
+The existing narrow suppression of duplicated runtime compaction output stays
+in place; arbitrary assistant text is not classified as lifecycle state.
+
+The proposed `agentCapabilities._meta["ai.ours/compactionSafety"]` advertises
+`version: 1`, `lifecycle: "completion_only"`, and `guardedCancel: false`.
+Complete start coverage and mutation-safe failure/cancellation coverage are not
+proven. A stream abort/reset does not fabricate successful completion or a safe
+cancelled terminal. Consumers reconcile unresolved starts after prompt failure
+or transport loss, and queue automatic messages until a usable prompt boundary.
+
+This patch targets adapter `4deace40379a62eb642559454930af4c590b3d49`
+(package 0.76.0), ACP SDK 1.4.0, and Claude Agent SDK 0.3.257. Deterministic tests
+exercise the real lifecycle and adapter prompt/status routing plus legacy
+regressions; they do not force live manual/automatic compaction or establish v2
+or complete runtime conformance.
